# MatchVaga Project Overview

## Product

**MatchVaga** is a SaaS platform that:
1. **Analyzes the gap** between a user's resume and a job description
2. **Identifies missing skills** required for the target role
3. **Generates an optimized document** (PDF/DOCX) tailored to the job

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router) |
| React | React 19 |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 |
| UI Components | shadcn/ui (radix-vega style), Base UI, Radix UI |
| Icons | lucide-react |
| Utils | clsx, tailwind-merge, class-variance-authority |

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── app/           # App Router pages, layout, globals
├── components/    # Feature components + ui/ (shadcn primitives)
├── lib/           # Utilities (cn, etc.)
└── hooks/         # Custom hooks (per components.json aliases)
```

## Path Aliases

- `@/components` — Components
- `@/components/ui` — shadcn UI primitives
- `@/lib` — Lib utilities
- `@/lib/utils` — cn() helper
- `@/hooks` — Custom hooks

## Design Source

Designs live in `design.pen`. Use Pencil MCP tools to read and implement from `.pen` files.

## Keeping Rules Updated

When the project changes, update these rules accordingly:

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New important library | Add to Tech Stack table; update `tech-stack-conventions.mdc` if it affects patterns |
